      "role": "user",
      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT\n- SIS_SUBJECT_CODE\n- LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL\n- TIP_DETAIL\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\n\n## Column Mapping\n- subject title: SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_TITLE\n- offering department name: SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- variance of the number of enrolled students: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- standard deviation of the number of enrolled students: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- departments that grant degrees: SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING\n- subject code description: SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.SUBJECT_CODE_DESC\n- count of reserved materials: LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG_KEY\n- total number of units: SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS\n- term '2009SP': LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.TERM_CODE\n\n## Join Keys\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID <-> TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ID <-> TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. For each department, what is the variance and standard deviation of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by that department, considering only departments that grant degrees and subjects with a non-null subject code description? Please provide the department name, the variance, and the standard deviation.\n```sql\nSELECT d.DEPARTMENT_NAME, VARIANCE(t.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS enrolled_students_variance, STDDEV(t.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS enrolled_students_stddev FROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED t JOIN SIS_DEPARTMENT d ON t.OFFER_DEPT_CODE = d.DEPARTMENT_CODE JOIN SIS_SUBJECT_CODE s ON d.DEPARTMENT_CODE = s.DEPARTMENT_CODE WHERE d.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND s.SUBJECT_CODE_DESC IS NOT NULL GROUP BY d.DEPARTMENT_NAME ORDER BY enrolled_students_variance DESC;\n```\n2. List the top 10 subject titles by the number of reserved library materials, including the subject title, the offering department name, and the count of reserved materials, for subjects offered in the term '2009SP'.\n```sql\nSELECT s.SUBJECT_TITLE, s.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, COUNT(l.LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG_KEY) AS reserved_materials FROM LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL l JOIN TIP_DETAIL t ON l.SUBJECT_ID = t.SUBJECT_ID JOIN SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY s ON t.SUBJECT_ID = s.SUBJECT_ID WHERE l.TERM_CODE = '2009SP' GROUP BY s.SUBJECT_TITLE, s.OFFER_DEPT_NAME ORDER BY reserved_materials DESC LIMIT 10;\n```\n3. For the top 10 subject titles by the number of reserved library materials for subjects offered in the term '2009SP', what are the subject title, the offering department name, the variance and standard deviation of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by that department (considering only departments that grant degrees and subjects with a non-null subject code description), and the count of reserved materials? Please provide the subject title, the offering department name, the variance, the standard deviation, and the count of reserved materials, in that order.\n```sql\nWITH DepartmentEnrollmentStats AS ( SELECT d.DEPARTMENT_NAME, d.DEPARTMENT_CODE, VARIANCE(t.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS enrolled_students_variance, STDDEV(t.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS enrolled_students_stddev FROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED t JOIN SIS_DEPARTMENT d ON t.OFFER_DEPT_CODE = d.DEPARTMENT_CODE JOIN SIS_SUBJECT_CODE s ON d.DEPARTMENT_CODE = s.DEPARTMENT_CODE WHERE d.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND s.SUBJECT_CODE_DESC IS NOT NULL GROUP BY d.DEPARTMENT_NAME, d.DEPARTMENT_CODE ORDER BY enrolled_students_variance DESC ), TopReservedSubjects AS ( SELECT s.SUBJECT_TITLE, s.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, s.OFFER_DEPT_CODE, COUNT(l.LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG_KEY) AS reserved_materials FROM LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL l JOIN TIP_DETAIL t ON l.SUBJECT_ID = t.SUBJECT_ID JOIN SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY s ON t.SUBJECT_ID = s.SUBJECT_ID WHERE l.TERM_CODE = '2009SP' GROUP BY s.SUBJECT_TITLE, s.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, s.OFFER_DEPT_CODE ORDER BY reserved_materials DESC LIMIT 10 ) SELECT trs.SUBJECT_TITLE, trs.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, des.enrolled_students_variance, des.enrolled_students_stddev, trs.reserved_materials FROM TopReservedSubjects trs JOIN DepartmentEnrollmentStats des ON trs.OFFER_DEPT_CODE = des.DEPARTMENT_CODE ORDER BY trs.reserved_materials DESC;\n```\n\n## Question\nFor the top 10 subject titles by the number of reserved library materials for subjects offered in the term '2009SP', what are the subject title, the offering department name, the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by that department (considering only departments that grant degrees and subjects with a non-null subject code description), the count of reserved materials, and the total number of units for each subject? Please provide the subject title, the offering department name, the variance, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), the count of reserved materials, and the total units, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers."
    },
